Shanling Q2 tools
=================

The Q2 runs Linux 5.15 on an Ingenic X2000 (MIPS32r2, nan2008, FP64) with
glibc 2.28, no IPv6 and no CA bundle. librespot runs from the card as a
Spotify Connect receiver next to the stock player, launched from the Rockbox
slot that Q2 Pod's boot hook runs (/mnt/mmc/.rockbox/rockbox), so testing it
flashes nothing.

  build.sh     static soft-float build and the card files, in
               target/shanlingq2/.rockbox (copy that folder to the card)
  launcher.sh  installed as .rockbox/rockbox: runs librespot | aplay in a
               restart loop, in the background, once per boot
  onevent.sh   librespot's --onevent: runs dacon when playback starts
  dacon.c      powers the CS43131 headphone DAC through /dev/shanling_dac,
               the ioctls q2-rockbox's shanlingq2_codec.c uses; demo powers
               it off after about 30 s with nothing of its own playing
  nan2008.py   sets EF_MIPS_NAN2008 in an ELF's flags

Build
-----

Rust nightly with rust-src (mipsel-unknown-linux-musl is tier 3, so std is
built with -Zbuild-std) and musl.cc's mipsel-linux-muslsf-cross:

  rustup toolchain install nightly --profile minimal --component rust-src
  contrib/shanlingq2/build.sh ~/x-tools/mipsel-linux-muslsf-cross

Static and soft-float, the binary needs none of the device's glibc, its
nan2008 interpreter or FR=1 mode. The kernel still refuses an ELF without the
nan2008 flag (the shell then reports 'syntax error: unexpected "("'); soft
float has no FPU instructions, so nan2008.py sets it. The tier-3 target ships
no crt objects or libunwind, so the link uses the toolchain's crt files and
its libgcc_eh as libunwind. TLS is rustls with webpki's compiled-in roots.

Device
------

Discovery binds 0.0.0.0 when [::] fails (this branch's discovery fix). Audio
is the pipe backend into the stock aplay on plughw:0,0, the CS43131 (card 0,
"ecodec-sound-card"; Q2 Pod's docs call it hw:1,0 when demo has opened
others). hciplayer holds the PCM while it plays, so local music must be
stopped. Logs go to the card: spot.log, aplay.log, cards.log, dacon.log.

Power the Q2 off before taking the card out: pulling it while mounted
corrupted the FAT once.

Status
------

Works on the device: discovery, a Connect session from the phone and audio
on the headphones at 160 kbit/s, decoded in soft float, with no stutter
reported. A headphone replug was needed once before sound came through.

Not integrated with the stock UI, which doesn't know librespot is playing:
  - its keys and volume don't reach librespot (the phone controls it)
  - its standby still runs: playback stopped when the screen went off
  - the DAC sits at -15 dB (dacon 70) under librespot's own volume
These need Q2 Pod's side: treat librespot as playing, as it does for
q2video (reset_poweroptions_timer, the DAC power), and forward keys and
volume to librespot. Bluetooth output is not wired up.
